A||N||6||Sndfr||Very dim gauge light...||||8||
Z||000000||Sndfr||12-03-2000||12:45 AM||||My gauge lights are so dim i can barely see them at night.  I can sorta see the upper left part of the speedo and some of the RPM but nothing of the middle.  The dim switch is at max.<P>Is it just broken bulbs or what? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  How do i replace/install new ones?<P>------------------<BR>-<B>matthew "Whyt Nyte" d.</B><BR>84 SE<BR><I>"You are not special.<BR>You are not a beatiful and unique snowflake.<BR>You are the same decaying organic matter as everyone else."</I><p>[This message has been edited by Sndfr (edited 12-03-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-03-2000||02:00 AM||||Check the bulbs first and make sure that everything inside is clean. Also check power connections to the board.<BR>The reostat isn't hard to change.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ur2biteme||12-03-2000||02:53 AM||||well, when mine was doing that, it turned out to be the alternator.  wasnt putting out enough power||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||12-03-2000||08:17 AM||||To change the dash light bulbs you'll have to remove the plastic cover that surrounds the instrument cluster.  There are several torx head screws (I believe they are the same size as the ones used to adjust headlights) in the face, along the top, along the bottom, and down low in front of the cluster (between the cluster and the dash).  Once removed you can look down between the cluster and the dash and see the backs of the bulbs.  They simply twost lock into the circuit board.  Tuern the interior lights on and you'll see hwich ones are not lighting up.  I believe the bulbs are 194s and can be gotten from WalMart or most any parts store.<P>If the instrument cluster cover doesn't come off easily don't force it.  You probably just don't have all the screws out yet.<P>I'm out of town and don't have any of my manuals or the car to look at for reference.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||11:14 AM||||  There are five T-15 torx screws that hold the rear cluster cover on, three on the top and two on the bottom edge toward the dash. Remove them, remove the cover. The lights are the twist lock type, turn them CCW to remove them, then pull the light out. It's a GE-194 bulb. your entire cluster contains 16 of them and they run about $2.00 a pair at Auto Zone. Just take your time and examine every thing real good, look for any breaks in the contact strips on the back of the cluster. That's all!<P> Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||12-03-2000||11:49 AM||||Bam, you forgot the two on the bottom.<P>There's two more 7mm bolts/screws on the underside of the cluster that hold the rear cover on. <P>You might also want to double check the contacts on the sockets and the curcuit sheet.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||01:14 PM|||| DOH! I hate it when I do that. Sorry, yes check the two under the bottom corners. SORRY, SORRY, SORRY. Bad BAM-BAM, BAD!!!<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
